---
layout: layouts/flyer.njk
title: Leaflet
permalink: /flyer/
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
<div class="sheet">

  <div class="mast">
    <img src="/assets/logo@3x.png" alt="{{ site.name }}" />
    <p class="mast-area">{{ site.tagline }}<br />{{ site.areas | join(" · ") }}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mast-rule"></div>

  <h1 class="hook">Computer playing up?<br /><em>We'll come and sort it.</em></h1>
  <p class="hook-sub">
    Friendly, patient IT help at home, explained in plain English and at a fixed
    price.
  </p>

  <div class="promises">
    <div class="promise">No fix,<br />no fee</div>
    <div class="promise">No call-out<br />charge</div>
    <div class="promise">Plain English,<br />no jargon</div>
    <div class="promise">Evenings &amp;<br />weekends</div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="services-head">What we can help with</h2>
  <p class="services-note">We can help you with any IT requirements. Just get in
    touch. Below are a subset of common fixed price services with indicative times.</p>

  <div class="cats">
    {% for group in pricelist.groups %}
    <div class="cat">
      <h3>{{ group.name }}</h3>
      {% if group.flyerBlurb or group.blurb %}<p class="cat-blurb">{{ group.flyerBlurb or group.blurb }}</p>{% endif %}
      <ul>
        {% for item in group.items %}
        <li><span class="t">{{ item.time }}</span><span class="l">{{ item.label }}{% if item.addon %} <span class="addon">({{ item.addon }})</span>{% endif %}</span></li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <div class="cta">
    <p class="cta-lead">Prices, offers and booking</p>
    <p class="cta-site">{{ site.url }}</p>
    <p class="cta-rest">
      WhatsApp {{ site.phoneDisplay }} &nbsp;·&nbsp; {{ site.email }}
    </p>
    <p class="cta-fee">A small booking fee confirms your slot — and it comes off your bill.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="smallprint">
    Times are typical, not fixed. Check our website for current deals &amp; prices.<br />
    {{ site.legalName }} · Company {{ site.companyNumber }}
  </p>

</div>

{# Side two — the business reader. Same bones, different promises: a business
   buys published prices, one accountable engineer and the 2008 heritage, not
   patience. Printed duplex this is the reverse of the home side. #}
<div class="sheet sheet-break">

  <div class="mast">
    <img src="/assets/logo@3x.png" alt="{{ site.name }}" />
    <p class="mast-area">Business IT support<br />{{ site.areas | join(" · ") }}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mast-rule"></div>

  <h1 class="hook">IT that just works,<br /><em>priced before we start.</em></h1>
  <p class="hook-sub">
    Fixed prices for the jobs small businesses actually need — published on our
    website, so you know the cost before you call.
  </p>

  <div class="promises">
    <div class="promise">Fixed prices,<br />published</div>
    <div class="promise">No call-out<br />charge</div>
    <div class="promise">One engineer,<br />start to finish</div>
    <div class="promise">Since<br />2008</div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="services-head">What we do for businesses</h2>
  <p class="services-note">Every job below has one fixed price and the time it
    should take. Current prices, the full list and online booking are on our
    website — printed prices go stale; the website never does.</p>

  <div class="cats">
    {% for group in businessprices.groups %}
    <div class="cat">
      <h3>{{ group.name }}</h3>
      <ul>
        {% for item in group.items %}
        <li><span class="t">{{ item.time }}</span><span class="l">{{ item.label }}{% if item.addon %} <span class="addon">({{ item.addon }})</span>{% endif %}</span></li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <div class="cta">
    <p class="cta-lead">Prices, details and online booking</p>
    <p class="cta-site">{{ site.url }}</p>
    <p class="cta-rest">
      {{ site.phoneDisplay }} &nbsp;·&nbsp; {{ site.email }}
    </p>
    <p class="cta-fee">Ongoing cover available on a support plan — ask about plans.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="smallprint">
    All prices are on our website. Migrations and larger projects quoted up front.<br />
    The IT Surgery name has been ours since 2008 · {{ site.legalName }} · Company {{ site.companyNumber }}
  </p>

</div>
